    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What battery standard does Africa use for trucks?</h3>
      <p>Most of Sub-Saharan Africa runs JIS N-series batteries (N150/N200, models 145G51/190H52) on Japanese, Korean and Chinese heavy trucks, with DIN/EN batteries (DIN88/DIN100) on European vehicles in North Africa and South Africa. Match the battery to the vehicle, not the region alone.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What battery stresses matter most in African conditions?</h3>
      <p>Heat, dusty unpaved roads and rough vibration dominate. High temperatures age batteries faster and increase water loss; dust can bridge terminals and drain current; rough terrain transmits constant vibration. Robust thick-plate construction and secure hold-downs matter.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What certification does a battery need to enter African markets?</h3>
